        k: 'Two pointers replaces an O(n²) pair search with O(n) by exploiting monotonicity: when the data is sorted, moving a pointer inward strictly changes the sum in a known direction, so the discarded pairs are provably not answers. The variants matter: opposite-end (pair sums, container-with-most-water, palindrome checks), same-direction fast/slow (cycle detection, in-place dedup, partitioning), and the merge pattern (two sorted inputs consumed together). The precondition is nearly always sortedness or some monotone property — without it the elimination argument collapses.',
