        k: 'One-dimensional DP indexes state by position, with transitions reaching back a fixed distance. The canonical family: climbing stairs (dp[i] = dp[i−1] + dp[i−2]), house robber (dp[i] = max(dp[i−1], dp[i−2] + a[i]) — the constraint forces the skip), max subarray/Kadane (dp[i] = max(a[i], dp[i−1] + a[i])), and jump games. When transitions only look back k positions, the array collapses to k variables and space becomes O(1). When they look back arbitrarily far, the naive transition is O(n) per state and you need a monotonic deque or a segment tree to keep it O(log n) or O(1) amortised.',
