        k: 'Unbounded knapsack allows unlimited copies, so the 1D loop runs ASCENDING — dp[w] may legitimately reuse the current item. Two distinct problems share this shape and must not be confused: MINIMUM coins (dp[amount] = min over coins of dp[amount − c] + 1, initialised to infinity) and COUNTING combinations (dp[amount] += dp[amount − c]). For counting, loop order determines meaning: coins outer, amount inner counts COMBINATIONS (unordered); amount outer, coins inner counts PERMUTATIONS (ordered). Greedy is optimal only for canonical coin systems — real currencies happen to be canonical, which is why the greedy instinct feels right and fails on [1, 3, 4].',
